From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cumin <13809292481@163.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:04:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] esp32: add ESP32-S31 support (micropython#19726).

The ESP32-S31 commits of micropython/micropython#19726 at 0b9512f475bd
(8634a282a..0b9512f47), squashed and rebased onto the previous patch: the
ESP32_GENERIC_S31 board, the S31 pin, ADC, touch and LDO tables, its
partition table and its component lockfile.

Two changes from upstream's. TinyUSB is the component registry's 0.19.0~3,
as upstream's, which builds for the S31; MicroPython's 0.21 tag doesn't.
And ports/esp32/usb.c gives only the S31 the UTMI PHY: upstream's also
moves the P4 to it, where the overlay's patch 0032 keeps a P4 device on the
full-speed PHY.
